ok - ship launch with no allowlist starts its agent with the compact-adviser switch on
ok - ship launch under an enabled allowlist keeps the compact-adviser switch through the cleared environment
ok - the launch command sets the switch on its own, whichever allowlist posture is in force
ok - a secondmate launch carries the compact-adviser switch in both allowlist postures
ok - ship and secondmate launches export their absolute steering inbox as FM_TASK_INBOX
ok - ship, scout and secondmate launches name the task's own browser session
ok - relaunch rebuilds the compact-adviser switch for the replacement agent in both allowlist postures
ok - a compound raw launch-command still starts its agent with the compact-adviser switch on
